<title>USA: Vermont lawmakers want 5 pct pay raise in 1999.</title>
<headline>Vermont lawmakers want 5 pct pay raise in 1999.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Members of the Vermont House of Representatives voted Tuesday for a five percent raise starting with the 1999 legislative session.</p>
<p>Lawmakers are prohibited from raising their pay directly, but are responsible for determining the next session's pay.</p>
<p>Last week, the House rejected a plan for automatic pay increases for lawmakers. Backers of the bill say the new provisions give lawmakers a raise outright, in a public vote.</p>
<p>The raise proposal now goes to the Senate.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
